      "side": 1,
      "message": "I will add an explanation here.\n\nThe reason behind this is: if we do not specify a token to be used as \u0027X-Auth-Token\u0027 for the specified request, a token with self.user on self.project will be requested [1][2].\n\nSince some tests disable this user, change its password, etc this \u0027X-Auth-Token\u0027 cannot be retrieved and a 401 will be raised, even before trying to validate the \u0027X-Subject-Token\u0027 in question.\n\n[1] https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/tests/unit/test_v3.py#L460-L467\n\n[2] https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/tests/unit/test_v3.py#L408-L434",
